INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (240, 58, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<p>The effect here is \"Physical DMG Decrease - 68.4%\"</p>\n<p>This is a huge loss of damage. This means that if you have 2 batmen you''ll do less damage than 1 full batman with good defense reduction. (DR)</p>\n<p>Alternatively, here''s an example of doing&nbsp;<strong>extra</strong> damage using defense reduction</p>"}', 48, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (299, 68, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<h1>Magic Hell Mode Build - SB6</h1>\n<p>This is a summary of the most popular hell mode meta build, the magic build.</p>\n<h2>The Mythics</h2>\n<p><strong>Main</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Tao - level 12/15</li>\n<li>Watt - level 12</li>\n<li>Kun - level 6 (early wave clear if first legendary is tiger)</li>\n<li>Kitty - level 12</li>\n<li>Lance - level 12</li>\n<li>Frog - level doesn''t matter</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Optional</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Dian - level 12</li>\n<li>Drain - level 12</li>\n<li>Meow V2 - mostly for gold gain, ideally level 12</li>\n<li>Indy 12</li>\n<li>Mono 12 (yes, optional. You can destroy later if reaper/magician appears)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Having exclusive treasures on the main mythics helps a bunch of course. Also, it''s not recommended to use Dragon, only Drain.</p>\n<h3>Gold</h3>\n<p>You''re going to need a lot of gold to clear hell realistically. You''ll want to learn to stack gold as aggressively as possible. Early eagles and frog can support your bandits for more gold gain. You don''t really want to rely on frog as a wave clear because he''s inconsistent in general. But if you happen to get a Dian after using Frog to boost your gold gain from Bandit, well that''s awesome. Or you can keep frog to the end. Both can be good choices.</p>\n<h3>Wave Clearing</h3>\n<p><u><strong>Tao 12</strong></u>&nbsp;is the bread and butter of this build. He does really solid boss damage. His strongest move is not his ult, but his skill that has a % chance of happening every time you attack. Because of this, and Watt, building up attack speed is the core concept of this build. Watt will be covered in the boss section. Tao is extremely good at clearing waves though. Not only is he good at it, but he doesn''t take up space on the frontline because of this huge range. This means he''s popular even in physical/hybrid builds. You can just throw him down and forget and he''ll clear waves for you.</p>\n<p><u><strong>Kun</strong></u>&nbsp;can clear waves as well. While Kun is weaker than Tao, he can be a good summon if you get Tiger early and can''t summon Tao for a bit. He takes a bit of time to build up mana to to roll rage, but he''s a solid unit.</p>\n<p><strong><u>Lancelot</u></strong>&nbsp;is also a good unit to use because while he''s known more as a boss killer, with enough mp regen from Kitty Mage he can do really strong damage against waves as well, even at the lowest Safebox levels. Even at sb6 though, his contribution to wave clear is still very high.</p>\n<p><u><strong>Iron Meow V2</strong></u>&nbsp;is really strong. Even when running a physical build Meow can be a good choice because of a couple reasons: he buffs mana regen, and he doesn''t ever explode like Chu does. His damage&nbsp;<strong>is</strong>&nbsp;fairly similar to Chu''s damage overall as well so he''s well worth the summon. He synergizes well with Lazy Taoist as well because Tao''s ultimate is more powerful against bosses than his normal whirlwing ability.</p>\n<p><u><strong>Drain</strong></u>&nbsp;is controversial. People are often on the fence because of the high cost to summon him. But if I were to point out his biggest Pros instead of his Cons, they look pretty good:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>He summons using eagles - your most common support unit with the magic strategy.</li>\n<li>He''s the single most powerful unit in the game, with higher wave clear damage than Chu or Tao, and higher single target damage than Vayne.</li>\n<li>Board space is limited in hell mode. It''s usually worth the extra effort/wait to put a powerful unit in the few spots you do have.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>You do have to wait for him to hatch, but since you''re stacking eagles with this strategy anyway, you''ll find that you have 6 eagles all the time. He might only come in on the later waves, but in hell it''s often worth that wait.</p>\n<p>The Cons are pretty rough though. The big one - Drain doesn''t do much more damage than Tao does. Knowing that, Drain really becomes a luxury. If anything, Drain is more of a flex in the current state of the game rather than a legitimate strategy.</p>\n<p><u><strong>Frog 12</strong></u>&nbsp;is a pretty solid unit as well. If you happen to get one from using frogs to get more econ/attack speed, not only does he do good damage, but he does more damage at level 12. Even though Dian has gotten less popular over time, he''s still solid enough to consider bringing to level 12.</p>\n<h3>Beating the Bosses</h3>\n<p>While Tao benefits from attack speed, there''s another unit that really benefits from attack speed more than any other stat, similar to Tao - Watt 12. Watt''s playstyle is that his normal attacks, while very weak, have a chance to add +1 to his stack every time they hit an enemy. He gets really powerful when you pop his ult though. His attack speed doubles,&nbsp;<strong>and his attack increases by +5% for each stack he has.</strong></p>\n<p>This ability is extremely strong. Nothing in the game is as strong as a Watt that''s been left to charge for half the game. Especially because the higher you boost attack speed, the faster he builds stacks, and the quicker he unleashes those stacks when using his ult. This is made even better because it synergizes with Taoist, who also improves more with attack speed than anything else, and you don''t need any Defense Reduction for either of them leaving plenty of space for attack speed buffs like eagle and frog. Since your main wave clear mythic and your boss killer need the same things to succeed, it makes this a very easy and consistent playstyle.</p>\n<h3>Support</h3>\n<p>As mentioned above, the main support you''re looking for is attack speed. This is great both early and late game. It''s great for early game because gold stacks faster, and it''s good for late game so you can more easily rely on Watt and Tao. You won''t need any defense reduction for this build, so the next best thing after you top out on attack speed at 200% is mana regen. (Attack speed has no further effect once you get past 200% so if you do get it that high, you can stop building it up) Kitty Mage is usable here, especially if you''re relying heavily on Lancelot. However, you can also consider running a Kitty-less build:</p>\n<h3>Dropping Mana Regen from the Strat</h3>\n<p>An interesting thing about this build, is you can completely drop magic regen (Kitty Mage) from it if you really lean into Watt and Tao. Taoist benefits very little from mana regen, and Watt gains nothing from mana regen. Since those are the main units, you can win easily without any dedicated mana regen. Iron Meow is still a good summon, he does solid damage. Kun is also good if you get Tiger early.</p>\n<h3>Summary</h3>\n<p>This build is a great build because you can essentially run it with only Tao and Watt 12, and Kun 6, making it extremely affordable and easy to get into. There are also all the other mythics mentioned above, which will greatly increase your clear rate and lower the reliance on RNG. You can run it with and without Kitty 12 and Lance 12, which if you followed the first unlock guide, you should have anyway so you can experiment with both as soon as you get Tao and Watt 12.</p>\n<p>That''s it for this build though. I hope you guys have fun building towards the higher difficulties. It takes time, but it''s reallly satisfying to build towards it. Good luck on the grind!</p>\n<p>-GhidWard</p>"}', 31, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (300, 69, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<div class=\"text-width\">\n<h2>List of Exclusive Treasures</h2>\n<p>These are all the unique treasures that only their specific mythic can unlock:</p>\n</div>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Treasure</th>\n<th>Level</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">Ninja</td>\n<td>Level 1</td>\n<td>Reactivation Chance +1% for Assassinate. Ult DMG 1%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MAX</td>\n<td>Reactivation Chance +15% for Assassinate. Ult DMG +25%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">Iron Meow</td>\n<td>Level 1</td>\n<td>Increases Iron Meow v2''s skill DMG by 5%. Increases CRIT rate by 1%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MAX</td>\n<td>Increases Iron Meow v2''s skill DMG by 50%. Increases CRIT rate by 10%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">Vayne</td>\n<td>Level 1</td>\n<td>Tumble''s cooldown reduction effect increases by 10%. Increases DMG by 1% for 3 seconds after moving.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MAX</td>\n<td>Tumble''s cooldown reduction effect increases by 150%. Increases DMG by 25% for 3 seconds after moving.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">Watt</td>\n<td>Level 1</td>\n<td>5% energy returned after all energy is used. Increases ATK SPD by 1%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MAX</td>\n<td>50% energy returned after all energy is used. Increases ATK SPD by 10%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">Dragon</td>\n<td>Level 1</td>\n<td>Drain Egg Hatch Chance +0.1%, Flame DMG +10% &amp; Increases Skill DMG by 1%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MAX</td>\n<td>Drain Egg Hatch Chance +3%, Flame DMG +100% &amp; Increases Skill DMG by 20%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">Lazy Taoist</td>\n<td>Level 1</td>\n<td>Increases Razorwind duration by 0.1 secs. Increases ATK SPD by 1%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Max Level</td>\n<td>Increases Razorwind duration by 0.5 secs. Increases ATK SPD by 10%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">Frog</td>\n<td>Level 1</td>\n<td>5% chance to refund 1 random material on each failed curse lift. Increases ULT Damage by 1%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MAX</td>\n<td>70% chance to refund 1 random material on each failed curse lift. Increases ULT Damage by 25%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">Tar</td>\n<td>Level 1</td>\n<td>1% chance to summon a tier 3 Tar when summoning Tar that is not tier 3. Increases skill Activation Chance by 0.1%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MAX</td>\n<td>30% chance to summon a tier 3 Tar when summoning Tar that is not tier 3. Increases skill Activation Chance by 4%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">Mama</td>\n<td>Level 1</td>\n<td>1% chance to summon an imp upon kill with Fear Skill. Increases skill DMG by 1%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MAX</td>\n<td>30% chance to summon an imp upon kill with Fear Skill. Increases skill DMG by 20%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">Bomba</td>\n<td>Level 1</td>\n<td>Increases Workout chance by 0.5%. Increases Physical DMG by 1%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MAX</td>\n<td>Increases Workout chance by 2.0%. Increases Physical DMG by 20%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">Hailey</td>\n<td>Level 1</td>\n<td>Star Power chance increases by 1%. Increases CRIT DMG by 10%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MAX</td>\n<td>Star Power chance increases by 15%. Increases CRIT DMG by 30%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">Kitty Mage</td>\n<td>Level 1</td>\n<td>Increases magic DMG by 1% for 3 seconds after mana recovery. Increases skill Activation Chance by 0.1%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MAX</td>\n<td>Increases magic DMG by 15% for 3 seconds after mana recovery. Increases skill Activation Chance by 5%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">Batman</td>\n<td>Level 1</td>\n<td>Increases DMG by 1% for 10 seconds upon successful upgrade. Increases CRIT rate by 1%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MAX</td>\n<td>Increases DMG by 30% for 10 seconds upon successful upgrade. Increases CRIT rate by 10%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">Monopoly Man</td>\n<td>Level 1</td>\n<td>Gains 0.1% of the used MP after an ULT. Recovers 1% of MP at the start of a wave.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MAX</td>\n<td>Gains 5% of the used MP after an ULT. Recovers 20% of MP at the start of a wave.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">Blob</td>\n<td>Level 1</td>\n<td>Increases Devour Count by 5 upon Boss Kill. Increases ATK by 1%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MAX</td>\n<td>Increases Devour Count by 50 upon Boss Kill. Increases ATK by 20%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">Indy</td>\n<td>Level 1</td>\n<td>1% chance to upgrade to a higher-tier treasure upon excavation. Increases MOV SPD by 5%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MAX</td>\n<td>30% chance to upgrade to a higher-tier treasure upon excavation. Increases MOV SPD by 80%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">Lancelot</td>\n<td>Level 1</td>\n<td>Summon Lancelot with 1 Flame level. Increases MP regen by 1%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MAX</td>\n<td>Summon Lancelot with 10 Flame level. Increases MP regen by 30%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">Pulse Generator</td>\n<td>Level 1</td>\n<td>Energy charge increased by 10%. Increases skill DMG by 1%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MAX</td>\n<td>Energy charge increased by 100%. Increases skill DMG by 20%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">Ato</td>\n<td>Level 1</td>\n<td>Ult Skill Cooldown Reduction Effect increases by 1%. Increases skill Activation Chance by 0.1%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MAX</td>\n<td>Ult Skill Cooldown Reduction Effect increases by 10%. Increases skill Activation Chance by 5%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">Orc Shaman</td>\n<td>Level 1</td>\n<td>Increases physical DMG taken by curse-stunned enemies by 1% for 3 seconds. Increases skill Activation Chance by 0.1%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MAX</td>\n<td>Increases physical DMG taken by curse-stunned enemies by 18% for 8 seconds. Increases skill Activation Chance by 5%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">Coldy</td>\n<td>Level 1</td>\n<td>Increases number of Glaciers for Glacier Collision by 3. Increases MP regen by 1%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MAX</td>\n<td>Increases number of Glaciers for Glacier Collision by 20. Increases MP regen by 30%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">Graviton</td>\n<td>Level 1</td>\n<td>Overheat from power absorption +10%, skill activation chance +0.1%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MAX</td>\n<td>Overheat from power absorption +200%, skill activation chance +5%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">Zap</td>\n<td>Level 1</td>\n<td>Increases damage by 10% when attacking the same target with the Arcane Amplification skill. Basic attack damage increases by 1%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MAX</td>\n<td>Increases damage by 100% when attacking the same target with the Arcane Amplification skill. Basic attack damage increases by 25%.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">Rocket Chu</td>\n<td>Level 1</td>\n<td>1% chance to avoid explosion on Overclock failure. Reduces the number of attacks required to use skills by 1%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MAX</td>\n<td>30% chance to avoid explosion on Overclock failure. Reduces the number of attacks required to use skills by 20%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">Master Kun</td>\n<td>Level 1</td>\n<td>Speed of Spiral of Fire increases by 5%. Increases skill Activation Chance by 0.1%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MAX</td>\n<td>Speed of Spiral of Fire increases by 50%. Increases skill Activation Chance by 5%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">Verdee</td>\n<td>Level 1</td>\n<td>Ultimate cooldown reduced by 5%, skill activation chance increased by 0.1%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MAX</td>\n<td>Ultimate cooldown reduced by 50%, skill activation chance increased by 5%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">Penguin Musician</td>\n<td>Level 1</td>\n<td>Variation skill has a 1% chance to trigger a better performance. Increase skill activation chance by 0.1%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MAX</td>\n<td>Variation skill has a 20% chance to trigger a better performance. Increase skill activation chance by 5%</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Credit to Yosh and Jubilent for gathering data about the treasure system, who gathered the information and posted it all on the discord before I was able to add it here.</p>"}', 31, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (232, 57, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<p><strong>Every time batman does his heavy attack, he hits every enemy currently in the game.</strong></p>\n<p>Now look at this next clip where me and the other player both sell our stun units right after we had our stun perfectly set up.</p>"}', 54, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (227, 57, NULL, 49, 'single-image');
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (229, 57, NULL, 51, 'single-image');
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (386, 102, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<h1 style=\"text-align: center;\">Welcome to guide codex!</h1>\n<p><strong data-start=\"1068\" data-end=\"1159\">GuideCodex is a growing guide platform focused on some of our favorite games.</strong><br data-start=\"1159\" data-end=\"1162\">Below are the games we currently support.</p>"}', 6, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (342, 83, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<h4><img src=\"https://ldg-guides-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/1767821566457\"></h4>\n<h4>Batman 6</h4>\n<p>Batman is a useful starter DPS for when you get the Tiger Legendary. As you cannot control the Legendary you get from merges and roulettes, you want to have a viable DPS option for each Legendary. Batman is good early on as his ATK boost from his Bat UP passive contributes a good amount of damage. You want to target +11 to +13 for his passive. Later in the game as your <a href=\"sb-mg\">Safe Box</a> level rises, the Money Gun ATK boost will outstrip the impact from his passive. But until then, he is a cheap option (as long as you stop at level 6) who will be useful in the early to mid-Hard and early Hell.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h4><img class=\"mini icon\" src=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pics/unit/mythics/Rocket%20Chu.png\" alt=\"\"></h4>\n<h4>Chu 6<strong> </strong></h4>\n<p>Chu is the DPS you want for the War Machine Legendary. His Overclocked form has solid base ATK and great skill damage multipliers. Level 6 increases the Overclock chance from 35% to 50% which makes it more consistent. Chu continues to be useful in Hell and God (though requiring level 12 by then).</p>\n<p>Overclock Chu at bosses during the early to mid-game and immediately during the late game. His explosion on failure will deal good damage to bosses in the early to mid-game but will be negligible during the lategame. Do not leave Chu in his base form in the late game.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h4><img class=\"mini icon\" src=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pics/unit/mythics/Lazy%20Taoist.png\" alt=\"\"></h4>\n<h4>Tao 6<strong> </strong></h4>\n<p>Tao is the DPS for the Storm Giant Legendary. Level 6 unlocks his Eye of the Storm passive which increases his damage by up to 400% depending on how the far the enemy is from Tao. He is the strongest mythic DPS for Storm Giant and continues to be useful in Hell and God (though requiring level 12 by then).</p>\n<p>He starts off feeling weaker to most because his base ATK is not very high. But his skill damage multipliers are good which means that the sb/mg ATK boost benefits him greatly.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h4><img class=\"mini icon\" src=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pics/unit/mythics/Monopoly%20Man.png\" alt=\"\"></h4>\n<h4>Mono 6</h4>\n<p>Mono is an important support for this strategy because of how luck stone-intensive it is. Upgrading Lance''s passive to the max level will cost 20 luck stones (2 stones x 10). A side benefit is that Mono''s ultimate executes a normal mob which helps a little with crowd control.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>"}', 24, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (380, 99, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<p>This is the silksong guides homepage!</p>"}', 9, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (431, 112, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<h3 dir=\"ltr\">Get 1-2 DPS mythics</h3>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Unless your Epic guardians are all maxed at level 15 and you have a whole bunch of them. you&rsquo;ll need DPS mythics to kill the W20 bosses. That&rsquo;s how fast the hp scales up in Hard. W10 bosses? Killable with 1-3 Epics depending on guardian level and upgrades. W20 bosses? Either 10+ Epics wailing on it till 10s left or a DPS mythic. And even with the DPS mythic you may not get the early kill bonus if your stuns are not set up properly.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Secondly, there is the Dungeon to deal with. When you get to sb5+, you have the luxury of waiting till W30 to start clearing the Dungeon before it ends at ~W42-44. When you just start, you need all the time you can get to kill the 5 Dungeon bosses.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">That&rsquo;s why you ideally want at least 2 DPS mythics so one can focus on the Dungeon and the other can clear waves and bosses on the main board. Between you and your teammate you will want 2-3 DPS mythics but people can be prone to bad RNG on roulettes and legendary merges. Or bad teammates in quick matches.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">The DPS mythics which help in the early game are:</p>\n<ul>\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Sheriff &rarr; Hailey 6</p>\n</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">War Machine &rarr; Chu 6</p>\n</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Storm Giant &rarr; Tao 12 / Vayne 6 (Vayne is Dungeon only)</p>\n</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Tiger Master &rarr; Kun 6</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\">Don&rsquo;t Forget Dungeon (W21-W42)</h2>\n<h3 dir=\"ltr\">Continue to increase damage output</h3>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">In this phase, the priority is taking down Dungeon and increasing your Mythic DPS output. This can be rolling for a 2nd to 4th DPS, or upgrading mythic level damage so that your existing DPS mythics deal more damage. Often, upgrading a few levels of mythic damage will help your single DPS clear the Dungeon in time while allowing you to keep 2 spots for your Bandits.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"ltr\">Build up your supports</h3>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Once you have enough DPS mythics, it is then also time to start building your support board. Monos and Kitties for luck stone generation and MP Regen. Attack speed increase to increase overall board effectiveness. Defense reduction for physical DPS (both yours and your teammate&rsquo;s) should be at least 180 and preferably 200 by W80.</p>\n<p>After you take down the W40 boss, make sure to clear the Dungeon before the timer runs out. With that you will enter the late-game phase of Hard.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"ltr\">Burning eco to save your game</h3>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">It''s inevitable. Sometimes luck is bad and gets in the way of you setting up your ideal board. Maybe you have bad RNG on getting stuns. Maybe your Chus keep exploding. Maybe you have a 5% Epic Roulette summon rate.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">If you still don''t have a DPS mythic by W25, you need to consider maxing summon level and burning coins on summons to squeeze out a Legendary to get your DPS mythic.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Danger signs for when you might need to burn coins:</p>\n<ul>\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">There was less than 20 seconds left when killing the previous boss and neither side has gotten a new DPS mythic</p>\n</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Mob count hovers around 60+ for a prolonged period or continues increasing when above 60</p>\n</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">You or your teammate was relying on only base Chu and/or Frog for DPS and just exploded it</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\">Late-game (W43-80)</h2>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Once in the late-game, you need to assess your board to make a very important decision. What Legendary do you want to pick from the W50 boss reward to help you clear Hard?&nbsp;</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Here are some statistics to help understand how much Hard ramps up in the late-game:</p>\n<ul>\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">At W60 (including taking down the boss), total damage dealt would be at least 1.5 trillion</p>\n</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">At W70 (including taking down the boss), total damage dealt would be at least 4.5 trillion. That means twice as much damage has to be dealt in these 10 waves as the first 60 waves.</p>\n</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">At W80 (including taking down the final boss), total damage dealt would be at least 13 trillion. That&rsquo;s nearly triple the damage from W1-70, and over 8 times the damage from W1-60.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">A lot of that health will be from the bosses. So you need to be confident of dealing enough damage to the bosses. With that in mind, the following scenarios are in order of highest priority first:</p>\n<h3 dir=\"ltr\">Not enough coin economy</h3>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">You want to aim for 300k+ coins by W80. For sb3, that&rsquo;s at least 30k coins at W40 or 40k coins at W45. That&rsquo;s a very tall task and largely depends on whether you get a good number of Bandits at the start. If you don&rsquo;t have enough, you will face issues killing the W70/W80 bosses.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">To overcome this, you will need to summon Lances and Kitties to deal enough damage to the bosses. See <a title=\"Lance-Kitty Strategy\" href=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/lance-kitty\">Lance-Kitty Strategy</a> for more details.&nbsp;For W50, you should pick Sheriff (75% chance to appear). With Lance 6, that&rsquo;s 3 Lances with active swapping of the third Lance in when the ult is ready. Minimum 4+ Kitty Mages within range for their ult to benefit the Lances. With Lance 12, 2 Lances will be sufficient.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">With this strategy, your stunlock must be solid to have no leaks. That is minimum 3 Electro Robots and 6 Shock Robots on each side, mirroring each other in location to maximise stuns. Make sure this is in place as early as possible.</p>\n<p>Have this set up and you will deal enough damage to take down the bosses.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"ltr\">Slightly short on coin economy, have Awakened Hailey</h3>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">If you fall slightly short on coins but have Awakened Hailey (immortal form) unlocked, try to rush a Awakened Hailey out. If you don&rsquo;t have a Hailey yet, go for Sheriff on W50 (75% chance to appear). After your coin passes 50k, max summon level and summon to have Hailey reach max Star Power and to build up your support board.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">If possible, have 3 Kitties next to your Hailey to boost her MP Regen with their ults to maximise the chances of summoning Awakening Hailey.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"ltr\">Good coin economy</h3>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">If you do have enough coins, use the W50 reward to summon another DPS mythic of your choice. Between you and your teammate, you should have 5-6 DPS mythics combined. Focus on upgrading mythic damage after and filling out your support board. See <a title=\"Hard Unlock Order\" href=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/unlock-order-hard\">Hard Unlock Order</a> for the suitable DPS and supports.</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Only spend coins if you will still have at least 300k by W80. The thresholds at various checkpoints are:</p>\n<ul>\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">W40: 30k coins</p>\n</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">W45: 40k coins</p>\n</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">W50: 55k coins</p>\n</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">W60: 95k coins</p>\n</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">W70: 170k coins</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Max your summon level before spending coins to maximise the number of luck stones from selling excess rares, epics and legendaries to use to upgrade your mythic damage. Remember to keep support units you need (eg. Eagles for attack speed increase, Hunters for defense reduction for Physical DPS).</p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Alternatively if you have access to Indy 6+ and don&rsquo;t have a good spot to place another DPS mythic, consider getting a Sheriff for an Indy. If you are lucky on the treasure dug up from his ult, you can get a massive buff. Aim for the luck stone per wave, attack speed increase, and (if you have Physical DPSes) defense reduction buffs.</p>"}', 3, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (301, 70, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<div class=\"text-width\">\n<div class=\"text-width\">\n<p><strong>Note:</strong>&nbsp;When treasure level up fails, you gain&nbsp;<strong>+% increment</strong>&nbsp;to the base success rate, up to 10 times total.</p>\n</div>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Level</th>\n<th>Success Rate</th>\n<th>Cost</th>\n<th>Increment</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>1 &rarr; 2</td>\n<td>90%</td>\n<td>5,000 coins 🪙</td>\n<td>+9%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2 &rarr; 3</td>\n<td>80%</td>\n<td>10,000 coins 🪙</td>\n<td>+8%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3 &rarr; 4</td>\n<td>70%</td>\n<td>15,000 coins 🪙</td>\n<td>+7%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4 &rarr; 5</td>\n<td>60%</td>\n<td>20,000 coins 🪙</td>\n<td>+6%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>5 &rarr; 6</td>\n<td>50%</td>\n<td>25,000 coins 🪙</td>\n<td>+5%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6 &rarr; 7</td>\n<td>40%</td>\n<td>30,000 coins 🪙 + 1 Red Ticket 🎟️</td>\n<td>+4%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>7 &rarr; 8</td>\n<td>30%</td>\n<td>35,000 coins 🪙 + 1 Red Ticket 🎟️</td>\n<td>+3%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>8 &rarr; 9</td>\n<td>15%</td>\n<td>40,000 coins 🪙 + 1 Red Ticket 🎟️</td>\n<td>+1.5%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>9 &rarr; 10</td>\n<td>5%</td>\n<td>45,000 coins 🪙 + 1 Red Ticket 🎟️</td>\n<td>+0.5%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>10 &rarr; 11</td>\n<td>1%</td>\n<td>50,000 coins 🪙 + 1 Red Ticket 🎟️</td>\n<td>+0.1%</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<div class=\"text-width\">\n<p>Credit to Yosh and Jubilent for gathering data about the treasure system, who gathered the information and posted it all on the discord before I was able to add it here.</p>\n</div>\n</div>"}', 31, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (392, 102, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<h3>Coop TD</h3>\n<p>A cooperative tower defense game that rewards strategy and teamwork. While smaller than Lucky Defense, Coop TD has a passionate community and a surprising amount of depth beneath its simple surface. We&rsquo;re building guides that focus on core mechanics, strong team compositions, and strategies that work best when playing together.</p>"}', 12, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (234, 57, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<p>Instantly they overwhelm us. None of them are taking much damage anymore. They''re nearly at full health when they run past and start to surround the entire battlefield. We lost that game as soon as we sold all our stuns.</p>\n<h2 class=\"section-header\">How much stun do you need?</h2>\n<p>If you have enough stun, the enemies should be almost completely locked in place right next to your attacking mythics. A very common stun layout is to have 1 full stack of the epic electro bot, and 2 full stacks of the blue shock robot, and have the same layout on both sides. Below is an example of a stun layout that is very close to that.</p>"}', 56, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (379, 98, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<p>test</p>"}', 9, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (302, 71, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<h2>How to Upgrade/Unlock Treasures</h2>\n<p>Once you get a mythic to level 10 you unlock \"The Altar\". From the altar, you can spend Kitty Treats to get a random treasure for the altar. You can only have one treasure at a time. Every mythic also has their own unique \"Exclusive Treasure\". The Exclusive Treasure is the rarest treasure there is, but is always the best one, offering unique and powerful bonuses. Rocket Chu''s exclusive gives you a 30% chance to avoid exploding when you fail his Overclock, letting you attempt to overclock again. It also reduces the number of attacks required to use his missile launcher skill by 20%. So it makes his biggest drawback much easier to deal with, while also increasing his damage.</p>\n<p>When you hear people talking about treasures, and exclusives, this is what they''re talking about.</p>"}', 31, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (260, 62, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<h1 class=\"section-header\">Attack Speed Increase</h1>\n<p>ATK SPD is a very important stat, ATK SPD directly converts to attacks per second, which means 2 ATK SPD is 2 attacks per second.</p>\n<p>You may have noticed that your passive attack speed bonus increases the ATK SPD by a bit more than expected, this is because of a couple things:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Fairy Bow</li>\n<li>Treasures</li>\n<li>Pets</li>\n<li>Active Skills</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>All of these magnify the passive attack speed increases coming from Eagles, Tigers, Frogs, and Indys. The formula for increase in ATK SPD looks like this:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Base ATK SPD x (Your Fairy Bow x2 + Treasure + Pet + Active skill) x In-game passive attack speed increase</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Another thing you may have noticed from the formula is that Fairy Bow''s value is actually twice of what it says it is. Meaning for example, a level 1 Fairy Bow is actually a 16% attack speed increase instead of 8%.</p>\n<p>Because of the multiplicative effect between active and passive attack speed buffs, you will want Tiger Master (for Shout) and/or Penguin Musician (for Allegro) to further benefit from your passive attack speed increase effects.</p>\n<p>Note that Shout and Allegro stack with each other but not with themselves. Ie. Two Tigers Shout-ing at the same time will only contribute 20% to the calculation and not 40% but a Shout and an Allegro at the same time will contribute 40%. Hence only one of each is needed, which makes them a worthwhile investment for minimal population capacity.</p>\n<p>Keep in mind that these active skills have a range, so they will not be able to affect the whole field unlike the passive attack speed increases, and they will have downtime due to being a chance-based skill.</p>"}', 45, NULL);
