INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (283, 63, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<p>This quest points you towards using mg to boost your ATK. If you haven&rsquo;t already, read the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pages/guide%20https://luckydefenseguides.com/pages/sb-mg.html\">sb/mg&nbsp;</a>to understand the importance.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h3>Stage 12: Reach Lancelot&rsquo;s skill level 6 (via luck stones)</h3>\n<p><em>Reward: 10 Artifact Keys</em></p>"}', 68, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (340, 83, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<h3>How does this strategy work?</h3>\n<p>This strategy revolves around summoning Lances with your Sheriffs, one or two DPS with your other Legendaries in early to mid-game and spamming Kitties, Eagle Generals and having a proper stunlock set up.</p>\n<p>You''re looking at 2 to 3 Lances upfront by W60 to deal sufficient damage to the tankier enemies and bosses. You may need to swap the Lances to make sure any Lances which are out of range of the bosses can fire their ultimate and start charging again.</p>\n<p>In the early to mid-game, if you get other Legendaries you can summon one to two DPS to be able to survive until your setup is complete. Late game after the setup is complete, you can sell other Legendaries for luck stones.</p>\n<p>Ideally have 4-6 Kitties to boost MP Regen. You may need to swap the further Kitties in before their ultimate to ensure that it triggers while in range of all your Lances (and Monos). In the sample board above, The rear 5th and 6th Kitty are out of range (2 squares range, diagonally) of the Lance and Monos in the first column and would need to be swapped into a nearer position before their ultimate for maximum effect.</p>\n<p><strong>Have a proper stun setup.</strong> This is <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>crucial</strong></span>. Minimum 3 Electro Robots and 6 Shock Robots <em>each </em>for both players. If your teammate is short on stuns, you will want to invest in more stuns to ensure that enemies stay stunned within Lance''s attack zone. If you leak too many, you risk getting overrun as Lances take the same amount of time to kill bosses and mobs (ie. not very quickly).</p>\n<p>With your spare unit capacity, get as many Eagles and/or Tigers as you can to increase your attack speed (+5% each). If you have Frog unlocked, each is +10% attack speed) giving you a better use for Wolves and Trees after you have enough Monos.</p>\n<p>Mythic damage level isn''t necessary for this strategy, which is good as this strat is already luck stone-intensive from having to upgrade Lance''s passive. You can upgrade it a few levels early to mid-game to boost the damage of your other DPS mythics but it won''t be necessary lategame. You can use it to complete summoning of the supports stated above.</p>\n<p>Conserving coins also isn''t necessary for this strategy as sb/mg ATK boost does not benefit Lance''s passive. Hence from midgame onwards, once you have a decent coin stash (40-60k+ for Hard), you can max your summon level and start coin summoning to complete your setup.</p>"}', 26, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (255, 60, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<h2>Mythic Stuns</h2>\n<p>At first, these units are outclassed by the standard blue and purple stun robots. That being said, they have their purposes at higher levels and with their exclusive treasures unlocked. Grav is popular to get 100% stun lock in hell, Orc Shaman buffs physical damage with his exclusive treasure, and Pulse Generator has become more common in the top-level Korean Lucky Defense community as of late, due to having good slow with it''s exclusive treasure, and doing high damage relative to the other stuns for wave 20/30 in hell.</p>\n<h3>A Tier</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Graviton</li>\n<li>Orc Shaman</li>\n<li>Pulse Generator</li>\n</ul>"}', 50, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (391, 102, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/\">Check out our guides for Lucky Defense here</a></p>"}', 9, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (292, 66, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<h1>Intro</h1>\n<p>Hell mode is the next difficulty after Hard and it is a very big jump from the previous mode. In this mode there is no dungeon which means less space for summoning units. Bosses are much harder to kill and special bosses appear at waves 30, 60 and 80. The special bosses which can appear are:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Night Shaman</li>\n<li>Coldest</li>\n<li>Magician</li>\n<li>Reaper</li>\n<li>Doctor</li>\n<li>Meat</li>\n<li>Barrier</li>\n<li>Grunt</li>\n<li>Kitty Sorceror</li>\n<li>Worm</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For a detailed guide about bosses and what they do,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pages/hell-mode-bosses.html\">see our boss guide here.</a></p>\n<p>The total damage you need to deal to clear Hell is 10x (130 trillion) the damage needed to clear Hard (13 trillion). That should give you an idea of how much stronger you have to be to clear Hell.</p>\n<div id=\"recommended-levels\" class=\"toggle-section\">\n<div class=\"toggle-button expanded-button\">\n<h1>Recommended Levels</h1>\n</div>\n<div class=\"toggle-panel\">\n<h2>Lance 12</h2>\n<p><em><strong>(Minimum)</strong></em> Without Lance 12, you need to either have higher sb (sb7+) to attempt Hell or multiple immortals that you know how to consistently summon to keep up in the late-game to make any meaningful contribution to killing bosses.</p>\n<p><strong>(Recommended)</strong> Still Lance 12. There&rsquo;s no need to level Lance beyond level 12. Separately, it would be beneficial to get Lance&rsquo;s exclusive treasure to save on the luck stones needed to max Lance&rsquo;s Flame (increase hp % damage) passive skill.</p>\n<h2>Artifacts (SB/MG 5+/5+)</h2>\n<p><em><strong>(Minimum)</strong></em> At minimum your Safe Box artifact has to be level 5+ in order to have any chance of accumulating enough coins for your DPS to deal sufficient damage in the late-game or to spam summons to get enough Lances and Kitties out. Even at sb5 you will be relying almost exclusively on Lance 12 to be able to kill bosses. Reaper Dian can kill bosses in Hell but not if you ruin your economy to summon him.</p>\n<p>Money Gun level 5+ is for your DPS to be able to keep up with the scaling of health of the enemy waves and bosses.</p>\n<p><strong>(Recommended)</strong> Ideally you should be sb/mg 6/6 which enables you to more consistently accumulate enough coins and for the mg ATK boost to be better for your DPS to deal sufficient damage for the late-game. The higher your Luck Stone artifact, the more consistent your early game becomes as you get more luck stones from completing early missions to do epic roulette summons.</p>\n<h2>Epics 12+</h2>\n<p><strong><em>(Minimum)</em></strong> Your epic guardians are going to be your primary damage dealers in the early game. In order for them to deal sufficient damage to stay alive early on, you need them to at least be level 12. Even at level 12 you may need to upgrade epic damage level in-game to keep up with the increasing mob hp.</p>\n<p><strong>(Recommended)</strong> Ideally all your epic guardians should be at level 15 before you attempt Hell.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"early-waves\" class=\"toggle-section\">\n<div class=\"toggle-button expanded-button\">\n<h1>Early Waves (W1-20)</h1>\n</div>\n<div class=\"toggle-panel\">\n<h2>Missions have changed</h2>\n<p>The mission list in Hell is slightly different from the Hard mission list. Notably the following missions are not in Hell:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Blacksmith (Upgrade 2x)</li>\n<li>Collect 10 Luck Stones</li>\n<li>Collect 1,000 coins</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The following missions are made harder:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Sell 10 Guardians (up from 5)</li>\n<li>Successfully hunt Golem before W8 (was W10 in Hard)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>There is only 1 new mission (Flashback), which is coming back from having 99 enemies on the board. Due to this new mission, the optimal start to the game is to clear this mission immediately at the beginning. Wait for mobs to reach a number of 90-97(units have to pass 99) to start spamming summons. When exactly to start summoning depends on the level of your common and rare units. If they are maxed at 15, you can start at 95-97. If they are low level, you probably want to start summoning at 90 to avoid dying from having too many mobs on the field.</p>\n<p>The Golem Hunt mission is a lot harder to accomplish now since it has to be done before W8. Considering the first golem is summoned mid-W6 at earliest and the golems take a bit of time to walk to the middle, you need substantial firepower to take down the golems in time. It is recommended for at least 4 epics combined between your teammate and you to kill the golems in time.</p>\n<p>If you didn&rsquo;t get any, try merging units and selling all Rares you don&rsquo;t need. Otherwise, upgrade epic damage level to make up quantity with quality.</p>\n<h2>Bandits are still the core of your coin economy</h2>\n</div>\n</div>"}', 31, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (286, 64, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<h2>What order should you unlock mythics in?</h2>\n<p>This guide is written with the goal being the fastest path to consistently clear hard. Explanations will be given for each step of the order.</p>\n<p><strong>Note for context: To get a unit to level 6 it costs 115 stones and 23k gold. Level 6 to level 12 costs 940 stones and 188k gold. Level 1 to level 12 costs 1055 stones and 211k gold. This guide was written with these things in mind.</strong></p>\n<h3>Recap of&nbsp;<a href=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pages/normal-mode.html\">Normal List</a></h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Hailey - level 6</li>\n<li>Master Kun - level 6</li>\n<li>Rocket Chu - level 6</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Building for Hard</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Lazy Taoist - Level 12</li>\n<li>Kitty Mage - Level 6</li>\n<li>Lancelot - Level 6</li>\n<li>Monopoly Man - Level 6</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Making Hard More Consistent</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Hailey - Level 12</li>\n<li>Kitty Mage - Level 12</li>\n<li>Rocket Chu - Level 12</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>Quick Note About Hard Mode Dungeon:</h3>\n<p>In hard mode, one early challenge you''ll face is how to clear dungeon. Honestly, as long as you spend some luck stones throughout the game on upgrading you mythic damage, all of these units will clear dungeon:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Rocket Chu</li>\n<li>Hailey</li>\n<li>Master Kun</li>\n<li>Tao (level 12)</li>\n</ul>"}', 45, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (279, 63, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<p>Farming coins is really important for sb/mg ATK boosting. Bandit&rsquo;s Loot skill is the primary means of farming coins early on before sb&rsquo;s effect dwarfs it once your coins reach sizeable levels. You ideally want to aim for 6-9 Bandits on the board farming coins for you in the early game, but don&rsquo;t summon beyond 80 summon cost (or 60 if you&rsquo;re more conservative). If you&rsquo;re unlucky on Bandits, you just have to settle for how many you have and let them farm whatever coins they can for you.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h3>Stage 10: Earn 500 coins from the Safe Box Effect</h3>\n<p><em>Reward: Money Gun x1 (Artifact)</em></p>"}', 64, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (254, 60, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<h2 class=\"section-header\">Support</h2>\n<p>Support mythics do things other than dealing damage. Some are strictly support, like Kitty Mage. Some are hybrid, like Iron Meow. But they add a different value to the team. Kitty Mage and Iron Meow increase MP Regen. Monopoly Man gives lucky coin generation and Defense Reduce. Stun mythics also belong here, such as Orc Shaman.</p>\n<h3>S Tier</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Kitty Mage (Get this to level 12 as soon as possible!)</li>\n<li>Indy</li>\n<li>Monopoly Man</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>A Tier</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Orc Shaman</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>B Tier</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Coldy</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>D Tier</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Mama</li>\n</ul>"}', 49, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (352, 59, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<p><iframe title=\"YouTube video player\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/mkx2Jiq4KCA?si=P_LCb3YDY989_gHj\" width=\"560\" height=\"315\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer;\n                            autoplay;\n                            clipboard-write;\n                            encrypted-media;\n                            gyroscope;\n                            picture-in-picture;\n                            web-share;\" allowfullscreen=\"allowfullscreen\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\"></iframe></p>"}', 20, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (256, 60, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<h2 class=\"section-header\">Conclusion</h2>\n<p>These are the main categories in the game. Keep them in mind when choosing between mythics to summon. If you have Wave Clear covered, consider trying to get more boss focused DPS. If both are covered, you can scale them into the late game by adding some support units. Try different blends of units. Even months into the game you''re likely to find units you had thought were useless in the past are good under the right circumstances. Understand the full kit of mythics and you''ll find the game leans less on luck, and more on an understanding of what to do with the tools you''re given.</p>\n<p>Good luck!</p>"}', 51, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (265, 63, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<p>Merging guardians is done by having 3 of the same guardian (epic or lower) which can then be merged using the merge button to get you a random guardian one tier higher (common -&gt; rare -&gt; epic -&gt; legendary). Merging guardians is important to make use of the excess common guardians you will get early on, and especially important for merging epics into legendaries to be able to summon DPS mythics.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h3>Stage 3: Clear Missions 5 times</h3>\n<p><em>Reward: 5 Artifact Keys</em></p>"}', 50, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (261, 63, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<h2>Help I''m New! Guide Quests&nbsp;</h2>\n<p>For new players, the game has a series of tutorial quests to help players learn the mechanics of the game. Here we will talk about the importance of each activity to your gameplay in the tutorial quests. Each tutorial quest has to be completed in Coop mode and within a single game. Completing one will unlock the next stage.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h3>Stage 1: Upgrade guardians 8 times</h3>\n<p><em>Reward: 90 Invitations</em></p>"}', 45, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (242, 59, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<h2 class=\"section-header\">What does sb/mg stand for?</h2>\n<p>Sb/mg stands for \"Safe Box and Money Gun\". These are artifacts you can unlock with keys. When you see people say \"You need at least 7/7 sb/mg for hell mode\" for example, what they''re saying is to clear hell mode you need your Safe Box and Money Gun artifacts to both be at least level 7.</p>"}', 45, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (258, 61, NULL, 47, 'single-image');
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (329, 82, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<h2><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">25 Million Run</span></h2>\n<p><iframe title=\"YouTube video player\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/OuOgq0OfIpI?si=iEEs-UfJX4tMkd1q\" width=\"560\" height=\"315\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer;\n                            autoplay;\n                            clipboard-write;\n                            encrypted-media;\n                            gyroscope;\n                            picture-in-picture;\n                            web-share;\" allowfullscreen=\"allowfullscreen\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\"></iframe></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h2><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Gameplay with narration:</span></h2>\n<p><iframe title=\"YouTube video player\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/yyZnSjRXj9Q?si=_d0CgEtNOlO27cjH\" width=\"560\" height=\"315\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer;\n                            autoplay;\n                            clipboard-write;\n                            encrypted-media;\n                            gyroscope;\n                            picture-in-picture;\n                            web-share;\" allowfullscreen=\"allowfullscreen\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\"></iframe></p>"}', 26, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (241, 58, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<h2 class=\"section-header\">How can I reduce enemy defense?</h2>\n<p>To actually reduce the enemy defense is much easier than trying to get a second Batman, Rocket Chu, or any DPS mythic. Lots of non-mythic units in the game give defense reduction (DR) just for existing. These are the units most commonly used for defense reduction (DR)</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Hunter - 10 DR (15 DR at level 12)</li>\n<li>Monopoly Man - 20 DR (This is a lot)</li>\n<li>Electro Robot - 5 DR (This is a lot less, but you need stun anyways)</li>\n<li>Demon - 5 DR (7.5 at level 12)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>These are just the ones I''ve used most often to get more DR. There are other units in the game that give DR. I recommend getting familiar with all the units, and reading through all their skills. The non-mythic units are a very important part of winning runs in this game and are an important piece in learning to win runs regularly and easily.</p>\n<h2 class=\"section-header\">Summary</h2>\n<p>This may seem like a lot if you''ve just started playing Lucky Defense. However, knowing this stuff will give you an edge that most beginners don''t have. Not only that, but defense reduction is one of the most important mechanics to understand before you can start clearing hard regularly. Once you know it well, you could even try to carry people through their first hard mode clears, even if you have low artifact levels (sb/mg 1). I recommend getting Kitty Mage 12 though, as that will make beating hard&nbsp;<strong>much</strong>&nbsp;easier.</p>\n<p>Not sure what sb/mg means? Check out the explanation&nbsp;<a href=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pages/sb-mg.html\">here.</a></p>\n<p>Also see our guide to using stun placement to 10x your damage&nbsp;<a href=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pages/stun-guide.html\">here.</a></p>\n<p>Good luck!</p>"}', 50, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (275, 63, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<p>Stun is hugely important. Knowing how to stun enemies to keep them in the kill zone. Knowing where to place your stuns. Knowing how much stuns is needed between both players. Most new players often don&rsquo;t keep enough stun on the board. The recommended amount is 3x Electro Robots and 6x Shock Robots per player. Check out the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pages/stun-guide.html\">stun guide</a>&nbsp;for more details.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h3>Stage 8: Achieve 80 Def Reduction</h3>\n<p><em>Reward: Safe Box x1 (Artifact)</em></p>"}', 60, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (293, 66, NULL, 32, 'single-image');
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (304, 73, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<div class=\"text-width\">\n<h2>List of Pets</h2>\n<p>These are all the different pets you can unlock in the game</p>\n</div>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Rarity</th>\n<th>Pet</th>\n<th>Level 1 Effects</th>\n<th>Level 50 Effects</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">Immortal</td>\n<td class=\"img-cell\">Poseidon<br><img src=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pics/pets/Poseidon.png\" alt=\"\"></td>\n<td>\n<ul>\n<li>When 5 monsters remain until the max monster cap, executes normal monsters with 15% chance each (once per match)</li>\n<li>Increases DMG by 10% upon attacking Boss Units</li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n<td>\n<ul>\n<li>When 5 monsters remain until the max monster cap, executes normal monsters with 30% chance each (once per match)</li>\n<li>Increases DMG by 20% upon attacking Boss Units</li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"img-cell\">Party Cat<br><img src=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pics/pets/PartyCat.png\" alt=\"\"></td>\n<td>\n<ul>\n<li>Every 60s, increases the Final DMG of own guardians by 15% for 20s</li>\n<li>Increases CRIT DMG by 10%</li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n<td>\n<ul>\n<li>Every 60s, increases the Final DMG of own guardians by 30% for 20s</li>\n<li>Increases CRIT DMG by 20%</li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"4\">Mythic</td>\n<td class=\"img-cell\">WhaleKing<br><img src=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pics/pets/WhaleKing.png\" alt=\"\"></td>\n<td>Increases ATK SPD by 2.5%</td>\n<td>Increases ATK SPD by 10%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"img-cell\">Wooroo<br><img src=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pics/pets/Wooroo.png\" alt=\"\"></td>\n<td>At the start of each wave, has a 5% chance to obtain 1 Luck Stone</td>\n<td>At the start of each wave, has a 20% chance to obtain 1 Luck Stone</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"img-cell\">Drago<br><img src=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pics/pets/Drago.png\" alt=\"\"></td>\n<td>Increases CRIT Rate by 2.5%</td>\n<td>Increases CRIT Rate by 10%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"img-cell\">Ghostboogie<br><img src=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pics/pets/Ghostboogle.png\" alt=\"\"></td>\n<td>Has a 5% chance to obtain 5 bonus Coins on sell</td>\n<td>Has a 30% chance to obtain 20 bonus Coins on sell</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"5\">Legendary</td>\n<td class=\"img-cell\">Blander<br><img src=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pics/pets/Blander.png\" alt=\"\"></td>\n<td>Increases MAGIC DMG by 5%</td>\n<td>Increases MAGIC DMG by 20%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"img-cell\">Rockfish<br><img src=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pics/pets/Rockfish.png\" alt=\"\"></td>\n<td>Gain 20 coins at the start of the game</td>\n<td>Gain 70 coins at the start of the game</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"img-cell\">Salamander<br><img src=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pics/pets/Salamander.png\" alt=\"\"></td>\n<td>1x Free Summon</td>\n<td>3x Free Summon</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"img-cell\">Braveheart<br><img src=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pics/pets/Braveheart.png\" alt=\"\"></td>\n<td>Increases Physical DMG by 5%</td>\n<td>Increases Physical DMG by 20%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"img-cell\">ShrimpKun<br><img src=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pics/pets/ShrimpKun.png\" alt=\"\"></td>\n<td>Increases CRIT DMG by 5%</td>\n<td>Increases CRIT DMG by 20%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"5\">Epic</td>\n<td class=\"img-cell\">Sticky<br><img src=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pics/pets/Sticky.png\" alt=\"\"></td>\n<td>Increases ULT DMG by 5%</td>\n<td>Increases ULT DMG by 15%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"img-cell\">Helmster<br><img src=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pics/pets/Helmster.png\" alt=\"\"></td>\n<td>Reduces enemy DEF by 5</td>\n<td>Reduces enemy DEF by 15</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"img-cell\">Grassfish<br><img src=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pics/pets/Grassfish.png\" alt=\"\"></td>\n<td>At the start of the game, has a 10% chance to summon a random Common unit</td>\n<td>At the start of the game, has a 25% chance to summon a random Rare unit</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"img-cell\">Anthony<br><img src=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pics/pets/Anthony.png\" alt=\"\"></td>\n<td>Reduces CD by 2.5%</td>\n<td>Reduces CD by 10%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"img-cell\">Ballfish<br><img src=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pics/pets/Ballfish.png\" alt=\"\"></td>\n<td>Deals DMG equal to 2% of current HP to nearby enemies every 30s</td>\n<td>Deals DMG equal to 7% of current HP to nearby enemies every 30s</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"6\">Rare</td>\n<td class=\"img-cell\">Tube<br><img src=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pics/pets/Tube.png\" alt=\"\"></td>\n<td>Increases Basic Attack DMG by 2.5%</td>\n<td>Increases Basic Attack DMG by 10%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"img-cell\">Dandan<br><img src=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pics/pets/Dandan.png\" alt=\"\"></td>\n<td>Reduces enemy DEF by 2.5</td>\n<td>Reduces enemy DEF by 10</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"img-cell\">Coolie<br><img src=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pics/pets/Coolie.png\" alt=\"\"></td>\n<td>Reduces enemy MOV SPD by 5%</td>\n<td>Reduces enemy MOV SPD by 20%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"img-cell\">Leafish<br><img src=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pics/pets/Leafish.png\" alt=\"\"></td>\n<td>Stun nearby enemies for 2.5s every 30 seconds</td>\n<td>Stun nearby enemies for 10s every 30 seconds</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"img-cell\">Jelly<br><img src=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pics/pets/Jelly.png\" alt=\"\"></td>\n<td>Increases MP Regen by 2.5%</td>\n<td>Increases MP Regen by 10%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"img-cell\">Handsome<br><img src=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pics/pets/Handsome.png\" alt=\"\"></td>\n<td>Increases DMG by 2.5% upon attacking Boss Units</td>\n<td>Increases DMG by 10% upon attacking BOss Units</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"6\">Common</td>\n<td class=\"img-cell\">MonoCell<br><img src=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pics/pets/MonoCell.png\" alt=\"\"></td>\n<td>Increases MP Regen by 2%</td>\n<td>Increases MP REgen by 7%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"img-cell\">Chili<br><img src=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pics/pets/Chili.png\" alt=\"\"></td>\n<td>Increases Basic Attack DMG by 2%</td>\n<td>Increases Basic Attack DMG by 7%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"img-cell\">Sproutfish<br><img src=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pics/pets/Sproutfish.png\" alt=\"\"></td>\n<td>Increases ULT DMG by 2%</td>\n<td>Increases ULT DMG by 7%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"img-cell\">Clawsy<br><img src=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pics/pets/Clawsy.png\" alt=\"\"></td>\n<td>Increases DMG by 2% upon attacking Boss Units</td>\n<td>Increases DMG by 7% upon attacking Boss Units</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"img-cell\">Squibbly<br><img src=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pics/pets/Squibbly.png\" alt=\"\"></td>\n<td>Increases MOV SPD by 3%</td>\n<td>Increases MOV SPD by 13%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"img-cell\">Doughie<br><img src=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pics/pets/Doughie.png\" alt=\"\"></td>\n<td>Reduces enemy MOV SPD by 3%</td>\n<td>Reduces enemy MOV SPD by 13%</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>"}', 31, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (259, 61, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<p>MP Regen affects guardians who have MP-type ultimate skills (as opposed to cooldown type ults). When the guardian has gained enough MP, shown by their blue bar filling up, they will be able to use their ultimate. Guardians recharge 1 MP per second and 1 MP per attack.</p>\n<p>MP ultimates either cost 100, 200 or 300 MP to use. Note that Kitty Mage''s ultimate actually gives flat MP instead of a percentage. So it fills the bar by a lower percentage for ults that cost 200 or 300 MP.</p>\n<p>MP Regen is incremental so every % helps. There is no cut-off or rounding.</p>\n<p>MP Regen is especially important for guardians whose ult is important to them:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Lance: His ult triggers his % health damage passive skill 10 times, dealing up to 22% (or 33% if Lance 12) of the enemy&rsquo;s health when fully upgraded.</li>\n<li>Mono: His ult executes a normal enemy to give you 1 luck stone.</li>\n<li>Hailey (with Awakened Hailey): The ability to summon Hailey&rsquo;s immortal form is a percentage-based chance every time she uses her ult while having max (10) Star Power. More frequent ults mean getting Awakened Hailey sooner.</li>\n<li>Indy: The ult is to dig up a treasure that provides buffs. More ults mean more chances to reroll to a treasure you want.</li>\n<li>Kun: His ult gains him a buff between +1 to +99 that increases his ATK. More ults mean more chances to reroll to a high buff.</li>\n</ul>"}', 48, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (277, 63, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<p>Defense reduction is important to enable physical DMG DPSes to continue dealing damage as the enemies&rsquo; DEF increases with each wave. Check out the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pages/defense-reduction.html\">Defense Reduction Guide&nbsp;</a>for a more detailed explanation.</p>\n<p>The reward, a Safe Box artifact, is also hugely important. Read the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pages/sb-mg.html\">sb/mg guide&nbsp;</a>to understand why.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h3>Stage 9: Earn 100 coins with Bandit&rsquo;s Loot skill</h3>\n<p><em>Reward: 20,000 Gold</em></p>"}', 62, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (237, 58, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<h2 class=\"section-header\">The enemy defense stat</h2>\n<p><strong>Note: I will refer to Defense Reduction as DR later in the guide</strong></p>\n<p>In Lucky Defense enemies have a defense stat. Early on, enemies have a low defense stat. As the waves get higher and higher, the enemies that appear have higher and higher defense. If they have a high defense, you do less damage.&nbsp;<strong>They can ignore around 80% of the damage you deal to them if they have high defense.</strong>&nbsp;But if they have a really low defense stat, you actually get&nbsp;<strong>bonus</strong>&nbsp;damage.&nbsp;<strong>You can get so much bonus damage that you nearly double the damage they take.</strong></p>\n<h2 class=\"section-header\">Which attacks does defense block?</h2>\n<p>The defense stat of the enemies only protects them from physical damage. Some characters do magic damage. The most common magic DPS characters are</p>\n<ul>\n<li>King Dian</li>\n<li>Dragon</li>\n<li>Lancelot</li>\n<li>Iron Meow</li>\n<li>Lazy Taoist</li>\n<li>Hailey</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>None of the damage these characters deal will be affected by an enemies defense stat.</strong></p>\n<p>Defense&nbsp;<strong>DOES</strong>&nbsp;affect the damage physical characters deal though. The most common physical DPS are</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Batman</li>\n<li>Rocket Chu</li>\n<li>Tar</li>\n<li>Vayne</li>\n<li>Blob</li>\n<li>Bomba</li>\n<li>Verdee</li>\n<li>Immortal Frog</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Any of the damage these characters deal will be affected by the enemy defense stat.</strong></p>\n<h2 class=\"section-header\">How can you see enemy defense stats?</h2>\n<p>You can actually see&nbsp;<strong>exactly</strong> how your damage is getting effected by the enemy defense stat by clicking on this icon I''ve circled in green.</p>"}', 45, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (250, 59, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<p>So if you have 10k damage from the mythic damage upgrade, it also gets this 910% damage bonus on top of it. Using this, the information in&nbsp;<a href=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pages/defense-reduction.html\">the defense reduction guide,</a>&nbsp;good&nbsp;<a href=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pages/stun-guide.html\">stun placement,</a>&nbsp;and some practice, you can start to clear hard mode without being carried. It can be hard, but if your teammate also knows the fundamentals you will start clearing hard mode all the time.</p>\n<p>Good luck!</p>"}', 54, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (320, 80, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<h2>Hailey</h2>\n<p>In Lucky Defense/What the Luck, damage scales off how much gold you can stack. To really get massive stacks, you need the artifact \"Safe Box\" to be as high of a level as possible. The more gold you can get, the more damage you''ll gain from the \"Money Gun\" artifact. Assuming your Money Gun and Safe Box are low levels, you can still get a massive damage buff from Hailey''s star power. So much so that it''s comparable to having enough gold to get the damage buff you''d want.</p>\n<p>However, it''s still important to stack as much gold as possible. Don''t make the mistake of letting Hailey''s Star Power keep you from getting big stacks. Stack that gold, and get her star power up by the end. Don''t rush it, and it will help you a ton in the late game.</p>"}', 38, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (321, 80, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<h3>Conclusion</h3>\n<p>Anyways, that''s the unlock order guide for Hard Mode. For best results, you''re going to have to reach Safe Box and Money Gun 3. Once you reach that you''ll be able to clear hard mode a lot easier.</p>\n<p>There''ll be gameplay of this approach soon.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Good luck!</p>"}', 43, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (230, 57, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<p>When batman uses his ult or any of his strongest attacks, he''s only going to hit the enemies that are right next to him. So what if we stun all the enemies so that they''re all clumped together right next to batman? Take the following clip for example.</p>"}', 52, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (263, 63, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<p>This quest counts whether you have upgrading guardian damage in-game. It does not count upgrading your summon level. Upgrading guardian&rsquo;s damage in-game is important to deal enough damage to get through the waves. From the mid-game onwards, you will be spending some of your mythic stones on upgrading your mythic damage level so that your mythic DPS guardians deal more damage.</p>\n<p>In the early game, the Blacksmith mission (upgrade 2 times) can also be completed with a net gain in gold by upgrading common damage level once and epic damage level once.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h3>Stage 2: Merge guardians 10 times</h3>\n<p><em>Reward: 10,000 Gold</em></p>"}', 48, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (298, 67, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<h2>Hell Mode Boss List</h2>\n<p>In Hell Mode, every 10 waves you will get a random boss. At wave 50 and above, 2 bosses will come out at a time. Each boss has something unique about themselves, either having an active skill they cast to attack your board, or having a special resistance or health bonus. All the different effects are listed below:</p>\n<p><strong>Note: Bandit Boss was removed from all modes for now.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><img src=\"https://old-ldg-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/corrupted-bandit.webp\">- Corrupt Bandit: Steal 30% money each cast.</li>\n<li><img src=\"https://old-ldg-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/bad-shaman.webp\"> - Night Shaman: Draws a magic circle on random spaces, and instantly mutates the unit in those spaces into another random unit. The mutation is chosen from the same rarity of the original unit, and this includes units in their untransformed state as well as \"Imps\" that can only be summoned by Mama''s skills. You can avoid the mutation by moving the unit at that time. The timing is strict, but...</li>\n<li><img src=\"https://old-ldg-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/coldest.webp\"> - Coldest: Randomly targets a unit and inflicts the debuff \"Reduced Attack Speed\" on it. This debuff lasts for 20 waves.</li>\n<li><img src=\"https://old-ldg-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/magic.webp\"> - Magician: Red warning = cast red circle on 9 random squares, and after a few seconds, a meteor will rain down on the unit in that square and destroy it. Green warning = periodically selfheal and recover its own HP.</li>\n<li><img src=\"https://old-ldg-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/reaper.webp\"> - Reaper: A red circle will be displayed on several random units, and after a few seconds the units on those squares will be destroyed.</li>\n<li><img src=\"https://old-ldg-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/smile-doctor.webp\"> - Doctor: Randomly targets a unit and inflicts the debuff \"Blindness\" effect (causes attacks to occasionally miss). This debuff lasts for 10 waves.</li>\n<li><img src=\"https://old-ldg-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/meat.webp\"> - Meat: Periodically selfheal and recover its own HP.</li>\n<li><img src=\"https://old-ldg-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/barrier.webp\"> - Barrier: Has low hp but has a shield equal to 10x its hp. Skills dealing damage based on a percentage of enemy total hp deal no damage to the shield.</li>\n<li><img src=\"https://old-ldg-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/grunt.webp\"> - Grunt: Takes reduced physical damage.</li>\n<li><img src=\"https://old-ldg-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/soccer-kitty.webp\"> - Kitty Sorcerer: Takes reduced magical damage.</li>\n<li><img src=\"https://old-ldg-images.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/worm.webp\"> - Worm: Randomly targets a unit and inflicts the debuff \"Mana recovery reduced\". This debuff lasts for 20 waves.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>To see the full guide to beating hell mode,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pages/hell-mode-guide.html\">click here.</a></p>\n<p>Credit to Eunhaz for creating this list of bosses</p>"}', 31, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (253, 60, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<h2 class=\"section-header\">Boss Killers</h2>\n<p>These mythics don''t always stand out right away as being particularly effective. In normal mode, you won''t need them. But when it comes to taking down bosses in hard mode and beyond you''ll need them.</p>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong>&nbsp;Despite these units being great at killing bosses, the only boss killers that are able to clear dungeon are Vayne and Zap. The others won''t be able to clear dungeon.</p>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong>&nbsp;Many wave clears will handle a majority of the boss fights. In general, you''ll only need a specialized boss killer for the last few boss fights on the harder difficulties.</p>\n<h3>S Tier</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Lancelot</li>\n<li>Watt</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>A Tier</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Vayne</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>D Tier</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Zap</li>\n</ul>"}', 48, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (318, 80, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<h2><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Beating the end</span></h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Hailey - level 12</li>\n<li>Tao - level 12</li>\n</ol>\n<p>To get through the end of hard mode, you''re going to need more damage, and these are the best units for the job.</p>\n<p>As mentioned before, Batman isn''t so good for wave 80. Even at level 12, because most of his damage comes from his upgrade ability, which caps out at a certain point, and costs a lot of gold.</p>\n<p>Hailey and Tao both do serious damage at level 12. For now you can leave Chu at 6, because even at level 6 he does massive damage.</p>"}', 35, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (289, 64, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<h1>Summary</h1>\n<p>At this point, you have a solid collection of mythics which should be helping you to clear Hard consistently. To help you make your next choice on what to level up, you can refer to&nbsp;<a href=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pages/mythic-roles.html\">Mythic Categories&nbsp;</a>where I go over all the different mythic categories, and rank them/explain what builds they synergize the most with.</p>\n<p>Or even better, you can use these two meta hell mode builds I''ve typed up to help you choose mythics in a way that lets you build your mythic team in the most optimal way. There''s some overlap, but the two builds are</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pages/physical-hell-build.html\">Physical Meta</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pages/magic-hell-build.html\">Magic Meta</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Choose one of these two builds and you can quickly get a high level hell-ready build. The easier to play build is magic, but when played well, physical damage seems to have an edge. You''ll see many high-level players use a blend of both strategies. The idea there is to play what you get. Get a ton of eagles? Lean into the magic damage. Get a bunch of hunters? Add some Chus to the board and easily clear waves. If you''re doing a hybrid like this, it''s good to get Watt and save him for the final wave. If you''re focusing physical, Vayne will clear all wave 80 bosses including Barrier. Regardless, check out the two builds and it''ll be easier to choose your next mythics to level.</p>\n<p>Good Luck!</p>"}', 49, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (243, 59, NULL, 47, 'single-image');
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (285, 63, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<p>This quest is unusual as Lance is pretty useless in Normal. However, he will be vital in helping to clear Hard mode when your sb is low (ie. sb3-4). In Hard, you will want to max out his Flame skill level before the later waves so he deals maximum %-based damage with his skills.</p>"}', 70, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (297, 66, NULL, 44, 'single-image');
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (262, 63, NULL, 47, 'single-image');
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (381, 100, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<p>welcome to COOP TD</p>"}', 9, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (291, 66, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<div id=\"early-waves\" class=\"toggle-section\"></div>\n<div id=\"mid-waves\" class=\"toggle-section\">\n<div class=\"toggle-panel\">&nbsp;</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"late-waves\" class=\"toggle-section\">\n<div class=\"toggle-button expanded-button\">&nbsp;</div>\n<div class=\"toggle-panel\">\n<p>Before W70, you should aim to have on the board:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>2-3 Boss Killers</li>\n<li>2+ Wave Clears</li>\n<li>1 Hailey, ideally in immortal form or at least at 10 Star Power waiting for RNG on immortal summon condition</li>\n<li>2-3 Kitty Mages (4+ if running Lance &amp; Awakened Hailey strat)</li>\n<li>Ideally 1 Watt (more than 200+ stacks)</li>\n<li>200k coins</li>\n<li>Mythic damage upgrade 10+</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If not, consider to roll Lucky Stones or max summon level and do some coin summons for more Mythic units. After your board is finished, you can put all surplus Lucky Stones you get to Legendary/Mythic damage level up.</p>\n<p>Aim for Mythic damage upgrade 14+ by W80. For coins, aim 400-500k for sb5 or 650-800k+ for sb6+. That said, if you don&rsquo;t have enough DPSes out, keep summoning for them. 3 DPSes vs 2 is a 50% increase. 4 DPSes vs 3 is a 33% increase. You want at least 4 DPSes (with 2 boss killers) in the late game.</p>\n<p>Attack speed increase of at least +30-50% is good to have. Coupled with Penguin''s active skill, it will boost your DPS significantly.</p>\n<h2>Another special boss at W60</h2>\n<p>Be very careful of the W60 boss. If it is a Night Shaman, Grim Reaper or Magician, it stands the chance of ruining your board such that you can''t deal with the W70 and W80 bosses. Remember to swap your guardians away from the target zones for Grim Reaper and Magician. Choose which units will have to be sacrificed if there isn''t enough space.</p>\n<h2>Fill out your support board</h2>\n<p>DPS is important but support multiplies your DPS. Get the attack speed increase, MP Regen, DEF reduction or Atos that you need to help your DPS do their job better. Some people leave their Bandits till late (W65-70). That&rsquo;s an option but make sure to merge them by W70 to have time to fill up your unit capacity with supports.</p>\n<h2>Mythic-specific tips</h2>\n<p>Stack Watt (250+ energy) until you get to the final boss and pop his ult to clear it more easily, that&rsquo;s the main reason Watt is so useful in Hell. If you struggle in the final stages of the game, you can pop him even earlier, but it is not preferable since all those stacks would go away (unless you have his exclusive Treasure) and even then it is usually not worth it to trigger Watt early.</p>\n<p>Lance&rsquo;s Flame passive skill should be maxed by the end of the game. If you struggle with Lucky Stones to max your Lance(s), summon units on maxed summon upgrade to sell for stones to max your Lance(s). It is that important.</p>\n<p>Hailey should have max Star Power (10/10) and preferably Awakened Hailey form. If you do not have Awakened Hailey, summon maximum 1 Hailey and summon Lances instead with your remaining Sheriffs.</p>\n<h2>W80: The final boss</h2>\n<p>Unlike the W30 and W60 special bosses, the special boss you get on W80 is unknown to you until it appears on the board. And the final boss can be different for each side. It is absolutely possible for a W80 Night Shaman, Grim Reaper or Magician to wreck your board so be vigilant and follow the same precautions you have done for the W30 and W60 bosses. A reminder that immortal guardians are immune to the effects of Night Shaman so you can focus on saving your mythic guardians instead.</p>\n<p>Make sure your board is ready to trap the two bosses in the midlane and keep them stunlocked so they won''t trigger their special a second time. If you are using Watt, remember to trigger his ult. If you''re using Lances, make sure to have them next to where the bosses are stunned, with your Kitty Mages below them.</p>\n<p>Hope all the above advice helps you to be able to clear Hell for the first time or more consistently than before!</p>\n<h1>Epilogue: What about immortals?</h1>\n<p>Immortals can be as strong as 2-3 mythics of the same role (boss killer, wave clear, support). However, bear in mind that immortals have their own in-game summon conditions which can be difficult to attain consistently. You can count your summoned immortals as multiples of the required roles they can fulfil in the endgame board, but the required roles do not change.</p>\n</div>\n</div>"}', 45, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (339, 83, NULL, 25, 'single-image');
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (405, 106, NULL, 5, 'single-image');
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (288, 64, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<div class=\"tab-header\">\n<h2>Making Hard more consistent</h2>\n</div>\n<div class=\"tab-body\"><strong>Hailey - Level 12</strong><img class=\"mini icon\" src=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pics/unit/mythics/Hailey.png\" alt=\"\">\n<p>Bringing Hailey to level 12 is important for multiple reasons.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The attack speed increase at level 9 (which gets amplified by any attack speed increase in-game)</li>\n<li>Level 10 unlocks the chance to roll for her exclusive treasure (Stylish Suit)&nbsp;<strong>[important treasure]</strong>&nbsp;which increases the chance of gaining Star Power each summon and increases her Crit DMG</li>\n<li>Level 12 unlocks a new skill Seed of Light to contribute to her damage output</li>\n<li>Each level increases her base ATK which increases the damage/effect of her skills and amplifies sb/mg ATK boosting and mythic level upgrades</li>\n</ul>\n<br><br><br><br><strong>Kitty Mage - Level 12</strong><img class=\"mini icon\" src=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pics/unit/mythics/Kitty%20Mage.png\" alt=\"\">\n<p>When levelled to level 12, Kitty&rsquo;s skills increasing MP Regen get +100% effectiveness. Her passive MP Regen of 20% increases to 40%. Her ult restores 20 MP instead of 10 MP to allies within range. Note that there is a typo in-game for the skill; it is 20MP / 10 MP flat instead of 20% / 10%.</p>\n<p>With your current mythic collection, Kitty boosts Lancelot, Hailey and Master Kun by making their ults more frequent. Without Kitty, you will have a difficult time using Lancelot effectively in Hard mode (and higher difficulties).</p>\n<br><br><br><br><strong>Rocket Chu - Level 12</strong><img class=\"mini icon\" src=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pics/unit/mythics/Rocket%20Chu.png\" alt=\"\">\n<p>Bringing Rocket Chu to level 12 is important again for multiple reasons.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The attack speed increase at level 9 (which gets amplified by any attack speed increase in-game)</li>\n<li>Level 10 unlocks the chance to roll for its exclusive treasure (Emergency Stop Button)&nbsp;<strong>[important treasure]</strong>&nbsp;which gives a chance to prevent Chu from exploding when failing to Overclock and reduces the number of attacks required to use skills benefitting Annihilation Rocket</li>\n<li>Level 12 unlocks a new skill Annihilation Rocket to contribute to its damage output</li>\n<li>Each level increases Chu&rsquo;s already formidable base ATK which increases the damage/effect of skills and amplifies sb/mg ATK boosting and mythic level upgrades</li>\n</ul>\n</div>"}', 48, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (248, 59, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<p><strong>\"Increases the ATK by 0.91% of held coins\"</strong></p>\n<p>I don''t have the specific numbers on how much damage Money Gun adds to damage yet. However, it becomes very clear once you start getting 100k+ gold, that it increases damage by a massive amount. If we assume the damage is a specifically \"0.91% x each gold coins held\" It would translate like this -</p>\n<p>100k gold x .91% = 910% damage</p>\n<p>If the damage translates like this you can increase your damage by close to ten times the amount with 100k gold. Knowing this, you can try to weigh out the options better as you play the game. Spend a bunch of gold to get a second batman right now? Or save gold for more late game power?</p>\n<p>The last thing to consider, is that mythic damage upgrades stack multiplicatively with your money gun upgrades.</p>"}', 52, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (322, 81, '{"type": "richText", "content": ""}', 29, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (228, 57, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<h2 class=\"section-header\">Using stun to increase damage</h2>\n<p>Why are these listed as some of the best units? Let''s say you have a mythic that can hit an entire group of enemies really hard, but all the enemies are spread out far apart like in this picture.</p>"}', 50, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (296, 66, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<div id=\"mid-waves\" class=\"toggle-section\">\n<div class=\"toggle-panel\">\n<p>If you&rsquo;ve managed to save 40k coins by W40, you&rsquo;re doing fairly alright but don&rsquo;t spend your coins just yet. If your coin total is lower than 40k coins at W40, you want to try to postpone your summoning as late as possible to let sb grow your coin stash a little more.</p>\n<p>If you want to start maxing your Hailey&rsquo;s Star Power or you need a bit more firepower for W50, you can plan to max your summon level and start summoning a few waves before (ie. W46+). Hopefully you have 60k-80k coins before you start spending.</p>\n<p>You&rsquo;ll have to assess whether you need to summon to beat the W50 boss depending on your teammate&rsquo;s and your board. But you will have to be fully prepared for W60 as that&rsquo;s late-game and you cannot survive if your board isn&rsquo;t ready. Hence you have to be ready to start summoning a few waves before W60 at latest.</p>\n<h2>Build up your supports</h2>\n<p>DPS alone is not enough. Your DPSes need their supports to function optimally. That&rsquo;s MP Regen for MP-based ult-dependent DPSes, DEF reduction for physical DPSes, and attack speed for all DPSes.</p>\n<p><strong>MP regen:</strong>&nbsp;Lance, Hailey (especially when trying to summon Awakened Hailey) and Monos benefit heavily from MP Regen. Reaper Dian and Tao both also benefit from MP Regen but not significantly.</p>\n<p><strong>DEF reduction:</strong>&nbsp;Target 220+ DR by W80 for your Physical DPSes to boost your physical damage output. If you have Ato and/or Orc Shaman built up, their skills also boost physical damage.</p>\n<p><strong>Attack speed:</strong>&nbsp;The more the better. But make sure you don&rsquo;t burn too much coin and lose excessive mg ATK boost just to get a few more % of attack speed increase. Ideally 50% ASI and Penguin but potentially much more with Indy.</p>\n<h2>Hell Mode Builds</h2>\n<p>For more detailed pre-match preparation, you can view these two guides about Hell Mode Builds:</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pages/physical-hell-build.html\">Physical Damage Build</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pages/magic-hell-build.html\">Magic Damage Build</a></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"late-waves\" class=\"toggle-section\">\n<div class=\"toggle-button expanded-button\">\n<h1>Late Waves (W56-80)</h1>\n</div>\n</div>"}', 43, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (244, 59, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<h2 class=\"section-header\">Why are these artifacts so powerful?</h2>\n<p>Safe Box and Money Gun synergize together in a way that can give you massive bonuses to you damage. Below are pictures of these artifacts so you can see what they do</p>"}', 48, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (257, 61, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<h2>MP Regen</h2>\n<p>MP Regen is one of the buffs shared with your teammate. Shared team buffs are shown as icons under the board.</p>"}', 45, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (303, 72, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<div class=\"text-width\">\n<h2 class=\"section-header\">Actual Safe Box earnings</h2>\n<p>In&nbsp;<a href=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pages/sb-mg.html\">What''s mg/sb?</a>&nbsp;we talked about what mg/sb are. If you earned no gold from enemies or challenges and only earned gold from Safe Box artifact, assuming you started with 100 gold, this is how much all the safebox levels would gain if just let that sit over 80 waves.</p>\n<p>These are all pretty good numbers as is, but considering this is only assuming you have no other income, you can imagine how much more you''ll actually get than this. With level 5 Safe Box and good gold management, you can get up to 400k gold nearly every game. With lower levels, 100k is still easily reachable, sometimes even more. To see why Safe Box and Money Gun are the most powerful artifacts in the game&nbsp;<a href=\"https://luckydefenseguides.com/pages/sb-mg.html\">click here.</a></p>\n<p>Good luck!</p>\n</div>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Safebox Level</th>\n<th>Coins After 80 Waves</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Level 1</td>\n<td>4,956 Coins</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Level 2</td>\n<td>7,247 Coins</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Level 3</td>\n<td>10,579 Coins</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Level 4</td>\n<td>15,415 Coins</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Level 5</td>\n<td>22,423 Coins</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Level 6</td>\n<td>32,559 Coins</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Level 7</td>\n<td>47,195 Coins</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Level 8</td>\n<td>68,293 Coins</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Level 9</td>\n<td>98,655 Coins</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Level 10</td>\n<td>142,275 Coins</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Level 11</td>\n<td>204,840 Coins</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>"}', 31, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (406, 106, '{"type": "richText", "content": "<p>The first skill consist of him shooting a piercing shot that does way more damage, each 5 shots fired The multiplicator goes from 500% at level 1 to 2700 at level max with the skin (+100% each level)</p>"}', 4, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."Block" VALUES (437, 102, NULL, 1, 'single-image');
INSERT INTO public."Checklist" VALUES (1, 'Flea Locations', 2, NULL);
INSERT INTO public."ChecklistItem" VALUES (10, 'Shellwood 1', 1, 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/in-game-images/10.jpg', 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/map-images/10.jpg', 'Easy flea. Go to the location and it''ll be right there.');
INSERT INTO public."ChecklistItem" VALUES (7, 'Greymoor 2', 1, 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/in-game-images/07.jpg', 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/map-images/07.jpg', 'Needs float. Complete the arena in the building next to this flea to activate the balloons, pogo off of them to reach this flea.');
INSERT INTO public."ChecklistItem" VALUES (2, 'The Marrow 1', 1, 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/in-game-images/02.jpg', 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/map-images/02.jpg', 'Easy flea, no abilities needed.');
INSERT INTO public."ChecklistItem" VALUES (1, 'Wormways 1', 1, 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/in-game-images/01.jpg', 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/map-images/01.jpg', 'Need a key and wall jump to reach this flea');
INSERT INTO public."ChecklistItem" VALUES (4, 'Deep Docks 2', 1, 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/in-game-images/04.jpg', 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/map-images/04.jpg', 'Another easy flea, no abilities needed. Right by the fast travel.');
INSERT INTO public."ChecklistItem" VALUES (3, 'Hunter''s March 1', 1, 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/in-game-images/03.jpg', 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/map-images/03.jpg', 'Top of a room, easy flea.');
INSERT INTO public."ChecklistItem" VALUES (29, 'Deep Docks 3', 1, 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/in-game-images/29.jpg', 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/map-images/29.jpg', 'Needs clawline to open the room to access it. There''s a room with waves of enemies. After beating it, go up to the left to find the flea.');
INSERT INTO public."ChecklistItem" VALUES (5, 'Deep Docks 1', 1, 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/in-game-images/05.jpg', 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/map-images/05.jpg', 'Another easy flea, no abilities needed. Right by the fast travel.');
INSERT INTO public."ChecklistItem" VALUES (9, 'Greymoor 1', 1, 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/in-game-images/09.jpg', 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/map-images/09.jpg', 'Needs wall jump to access the top area of Greymoor. There will be fans that can be activated by hitting switches. The platforming section through these fans leads to a flea.');
INSERT INTO public."ChecklistItem" VALUES (8, 'Kratt', 1, 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/in-game-images/08.jpg', 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/map-images/08.jpg', 'Needs wall jump to access the top area of Greymoor. Behind a breakable wall.');
INSERT INTO public."ChecklistItem" VALUES (11, 'Bellhart 1', 1, 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/in-game-images/11.jpg', 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/map-images/11.jpg', 'Needs wall jump. It''s on the way to Widow, upwards from the path that takes you to her.');
INSERT INTO public."ChecklistItem" VALUES (13, 'Sands of Karak 2', 1, 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/in-game-images/13.jpg', 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/map-images/13.jpg', 'Requires double jump. Both fleas in this area are available by going through platforming sections and are easy to find. Follow the pictures of the map and you''ll go right to them.');
INSERT INTO public."ChecklistItem" VALUES (14, 'Sinner''s Road 1', 1, 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/in-game-images/14.jpg', 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/map-images/14.jpg', 'Another easy flea. Go in and break the cage for another flea.');
INSERT INTO public."ChecklistItem" VALUES (16, 'Choral Chambers 2', 1, 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/in-game-images/16.jpg', 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/map-images/16.jpg', 'Another easy flea. There''s a pit of spikes with flying enemies. Get across it and collect another flea.');
INSERT INTO public."ChecklistItem" VALUES (18, 'The Slab 2', 1, 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/in-game-images/18.jpg', 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/map-images/18.jpg', 'If you didn''t get kidnapped in your first playthrough you''ll need the key of the apostate to access the area. You can find it in the putrified ducts. After that it''s in a room to the left of the bench room.');
INSERT INTO public."ChecklistItem" VALUES (19, 'The Slab 1', 1, 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/in-game-images/19.jpg', 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/map-images/19.jpg', 'Double jump needed here - jump on the wall above the bench, then double jump to reach the secret hole in the wall in the top right.');
INSERT INTO public."ChecklistItem" VALUES (21, 'Memorium 1', 1, 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/in-game-images/21.jpg', 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/map-images/21.jpg', 'This flea is a big boy. Throw hands to collect it.');
INSERT INTO public."ChecklistItem" VALUES (23, 'Whispering Vaults 1', 1, 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/in-game-images/23.jpg', 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/map-images/23.jpg', 'There''s a simple puzzle where you need to move a box to the top to reach the flea. If you have double jump and clawline you can skip this, but you need at least clawline to reach it.');
INSERT INTO public."ChecklistItem" VALUES (25, 'Bilewater 2', 1, 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/in-game-images/25.jpg', 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/map-images/25.jpg', 'Behind a breakable wall');
INSERT INTO public."ChecklistItem" VALUES (26, 'Bilewater 1', 1, 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/in-game-images/26.jpg', 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/map-images/26.jpg', 'Top left corner of the room to the right of the flea there''s a hidden pathway.');
INSERT INTO public."ChecklistItem" VALUES (27, 'Underworks 1', 1, 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/in-game-images/27.jpg', 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/map-images/27.jpg', 'Go through the wisp thicket to get to the bottom entrance of the underworks. This bottom entrance has a flea on the way to the main underworks area.');
INSERT INTO public."ChecklistItem" VALUES (28, 'Underworks 2', 1, 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/in-game-images/28.jpg', 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/map-images/28.jpg', 'Through a room with exploding enemies.');
INSERT INTO public."ChecklistItem" VALUES (6, 'Far Fields 2', 1, 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/in-game-images/06.jpg', 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/map-images/06.png', 'Needs sprint. On the map, you''ll approach coming from beneath the room, up to it. There''s a room where there''s an ant you can fight, next to some stringed beads. There will be a breakable wall to the right. Go through there, follow the path, and you''ll reach the area with the flea.');
INSERT INTO public."ChecklistItem" VALUES (12, 'Far Fields 1', 1, 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/in-game-images/12.jpg', 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/map-images/12.jpg', 'Needs wall jump and float. This one is hidden. Go to the Bell Beast''s area. Walk into his little bed of bells, and walk into the wall on the right side. This leads to a platforming section that ends with a Rhino fight and a flea.');
INSERT INTO public."ChecklistItem" VALUES (15, 'Bilewater 3', 1, 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/in-game-images/15.jpg', 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/map-images/15.jpg', 'In the Exhaust Organ area. The hardest part is getting to the Exhaust Organ. You can go from Sinner''s road, through the mist, and you''ll end up at the Exhaust Organ, or you can go from whispering vaults, to bilewater, and to the left of the lower bench is another entrance to the mist, which will take you to the Exhaust Organ. To reach the flea you''ll need to go inside the building, and there will be a door to come back outside higher up in the building. Go to the left from there to reach the flea.');
INSERT INTO public."ChecklistItem" VALUES (17, 'Choral Chambers 3', 1, 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/in-game-images/17.jpg', 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/map-images/17.jpg', 'There are two breakable walls. The lower breakable walls lets you activate a fan. This fan will blow air up into the area in the upper breakable wall, allowing you to ride the current up to a flea.');
INSERT INTO public."ChecklistItem" VALUES (20, 'Mount Fay 1', 1, 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/in-game-images/20.jpg', 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/map-images/20.jpg', 'There''s a secret hole in the top left of a ceiling. This will take you to some platforming, with a flea at the end.');
INSERT INTO public."ChecklistItem" VALUES (22, 'Vog', 1, 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/in-game-images/22.jpg', 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/map-images/22.jpg', 'There''s an area where tendrils will grab you and pull you through the ceiling. This leads to a platforming section where you keep using tendrils to continue your ascent. At the end of the platforming tendril challenge you''ll find Vog.');
INSERT INTO public."ChecklistItem" VALUES (24, 'Choral Chambers 1', 1, 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/in-game-images/24.jpg', 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/map-images/24.jpg', 'In the whispering vaults theres a hole hidden in the top right of one of the rooms. This hole can take you either to Bilewater, or to a hidden higher area of the Choral Chambers. In this hidden upper area, if you climb the wall to the right, you''ll find a flea.');
INSERT INTO public."ChecklistItem" VALUES (30, 'Sands of Karak 1', 1, 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/in-game-images/30.jpg', 'https://checklist-images-guides.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/flea-guide/map-images/30.jpg', 'Requires double jump. Both fleas in this area are available by going through platforming sections and are easy to find. Follow the pictures of the map and you''ll go right to them.');
